b * (a / b) + a mod b)%Z\n\nArguments Z_div_mod_eq_full (a b)%Z_scope", "extras": {"command": "coqc /tmp/CompCert/test_coq3.v 2>&1", "metadata": {"exit_code": 0, "pid": -1, "username": "root", "hostname": "rack-ge107-ya-20250517193240", "working_dir": "/tmp/CompCert/CompCert-3.13.1", "py_interpreter_path": "", "prefix": "", "suffix": "\n[The command completed with exit code 0.]"}, "hidden": false}, "success": true}
{"id": 95, "timestamp": "2025-12-31T06:19:20.608670", "source": "agent", "message": "Running command: \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\ngrep -n \"Z_div_mod_eq\" flocq/ -r\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n", "action": "run", "tool_call_metadata": {"function_name": "execute_bash", "tool_call_id": "toolu_46", "model_response": {"id": "c58f2c95b1164b5a9e40daaf631c1dea", "created": 1767161960, "model": "deepseek-v3.2", "object": "chat.completion", "system_fingerprint": null, "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"content": "Great! So `Z_div_mod_eq_full` exists and is the correct lemma. Our change in flocq/Calc/Bracket.v should work. However, we also need to check other files that use `Z_div_mod_eq`. The issue is that some files might be using the local lemma from Coqlib.v. Actually, looking at the grep output, many files are using `Z_div_mod_eq` which is defined in Coqlib.v. The flocq library doesn't import Coqlib.v, so it can't use that lemma. That's why it was trying to use the standard library version (which doesn't exist as `Z_div_mod_eq` in Coq 8.18).\n\nWe need to fix flocq to use the correct lemma from ZArith. We changed it to `Z_div_mod_eq_full`. But we also need to check if flocq imports ZArith properly. It does import ZArith. So the change should work.\n\nHowever, there's another issue: the local lemma `Z_div_mod_eq` in Coqlib.v might be used by other files. That should be fine because it's defined locally. But wait, flocq is a separate library that doesn't import Coqlib.v. So it shouldn't be using `Z_div_mod_eq` at all unless it's defined somewhere in flocq. Let me check if flocq has its own definition.", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": [{"index": 1, "function": {"arguments": "{\"command\": \"\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n