ch doesn't exist as `Z_div_mod_eq` in Coq 8.18).\n\nWe need to fix flocq to use the correct lemma from ZArith. We changed it to `Z_div_mod_eq_full`. But we also need to check if flocq imports ZArith properly. It does import ZArith. So the change should work.\n\nHowever, there's another issue: the local lemma `Z_div_mod_eq` in Coqlib.v might be used by other files. That should be fine because it's defined locally. But wait, flocq is a separate library that doesn't import Coqlib.v. So it shouldn't be using `Z_div_mod_eq` at all unless it's defined somewhere in flocq. Let me check if flocq has its own definition.", "blocking": false, "is_static": false, "cwd": null, "hidden": false, "confirmation_state": "confirmed"}}
